<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Numayrids</h1><p class="st-meta">990 CE – 1081 CE (approx.) · capital Harran</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Arab emirs of the Banu Numayr who ruled Harran and the towns of the western Jazira for nearly a century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Banu Numayr were a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bedouin">Bedouin</a> tribe of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-amir">Amir ibn Sa'sa'a</a> who moved into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diyar-mudar">Diyar Mudar</a>, the region between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balikh-river">Balikh</a>. Around 990, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamdanid-dynasty">Hamdanid</a> power faded, their chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waththab-ibn-sabiq">Waththab ibn Sabiq</a> seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harran">Harran</a>, and the tribe went on to hold <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saruj">Saruj</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raqqa">Raqqa</a> and for a time <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-edessa">Edessa</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Numayrids were tribal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> who lived partly as nomads and relied on the townspeople and on dues from the fertile river valleys. They balanced between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mirdasid-emirate">Mirdasids</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/marwanids">Marwanids</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harran">Harran</a> still had a community of Sabian star-worshippers, whose temple the Numayrids are said to have turned into a palace. In 1031 they lost <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-edessa">Edessa</a> to Byzantine forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-maniakes">George Maniakes</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk</a> advance weakened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bedouin">Bedouin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirates</a>. Around 1081 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uqaylid-dynasty">Uqaylid</a> emir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muslim-ibn-quraysh">Muslim ibn Quraysh</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harran">Harran</a>, ending Numayrid rule; the tribe itself survived in the region.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/numayrids.jpg" alt="Numayrids" width="320" height="271"><figcaption>Image: Attar-Aram syria · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Numayrid_dynasty.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>990 CE – 1081 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Harran</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Waththab ibn Sabiq, Shabib ibn Waththab, Mani' ibn Shabib</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>, <a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Banu Numayr</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1036&amp;focus=numayrids" aria-label="Numayrids on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5659 849 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Numayrids lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5979 1105L5811 1337M5979 1105L6481 1127"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5811 1337h0M6481 1127h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5979 1105h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5979 1105h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Harran. <a href="/atlas?year=1036&amp;focus=numayrids">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

